{"author":"Rebar Bot Nava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"lowfat-hydrated-koalabear","creation_channel":"cli","description":"## Observation\n`sweep (windows)` on main at `8c6c4f29af8` (run 44636174645, job 135955149952): 20311 passed, 1 failed. The failure is `tests/unit/test_mcp_opcert_signing_goose.py::test_compose_startup_binding_fails_closed_on_bad_key` with `Failed: DID NOT RAISE OpcertKeyError`. The test passed in the earlier main sweeps.\n\n## Cause\nThe test makes the key \"too permissive\" with `chmod(0o644)` and expects the POSIX 0600 source check in `keyprov._read_path_source` to reject it. On Windows that check is skipped by design (`_POSIX_MODE_BITS`, decision cloistered-decomposed-nymph), and `chmod` cannot add group/other access. Before plump-smelly-indianabat (change 3462), the test passed on Windows only by accident: compose always failed, because `ssh-keygen` refused the OWNER RIGHTS key copy, and that raised the expected `OpcertKeyError`. Now compose succeeds on Windows, so the test's premise does not hold there.\n\n## Approach\nTest-only. Mark `test_compose_startup_binding_fails_closed_on_bad_key` with a `skipif(os.name == \"nt\")` whose reason names the cause: Windows has no POSIX mode bits, and by decision cloistered-decomposed-nymph rebar skips the 0600 check there. This follows the existing `_POSIX_ONLY` pattern in `tests/unit/test_windows_mode_bit_skip.py`. No product code, config key, env var or flag changes. The fail-closed behaviour on Windows stays covered by the other compose error paths (malformed key, missing source), which raise on every platform.\n\n## Scope\n- `tests/unit/test_mcp_opcert_signing_goose.py` — the skip marker.\n\n## Testing\n- On macOS/Linux the test still runs and passes (`make verify`).\n- After merge: a `sweep (windows)` run on main reports the test as skipped with the reason, and no failures.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] `test_compose_startup_binding_fails_closed_on_bad_key` is skipped on Windows with a reason citing the absent POSIX mode bits and decision cloistered-decomposed-nymph, and still runs on POSIX.\n- [ ] A `sweep (windows)` run on main after the change has no failures in `test_mcp_opcert_signing_goose.py`.","id":"d8f6-2168-06e7-4133","parent_id":"","priority":2,"tags":["windows","portability","tests"],"ticket_type":"bug","title":"Windows: goose fail-closed test assumed compose fails; it relies on a POSIX 0600 check skipped on Windows"},"env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1795135995058713001,"uuid":"c9ebddcb-09e3-41b7-bcee-d39ecceb127f"}